  "recipeCuisine": "Thailand",
  "name": "Steamed Sea Bass with Lime",
  "text": "Steamed Sea Bass with Lime\n\nPrep time: ?\n\nCooking time: 8-10 minutes\n\nTotal time: ?\n\nYield: 4\n\nStatus: Untried\n\nIngredients\n\n1 whole sea bass (approximately 450g, cleaned, scaled, and trimmed),\n\n5 green and red hot chillis (finely chopped),\n\n5 cloves garlic (finely chopped),\n\n½ cup chicken stock (or water),\n\n3 tbsp lime juice,\n\n1 ½ tbsp light soy sauce.\n\nGarnish\n\n1 lime (sliced),\n\n1 sprig coriander,\n\n1 medium tomato.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Score the fish diagonally on both sides and put on a plate.\n\n2. Mix the chilli and garlic with the stock and stir well. Add the lime juice and light soy sauce and stir again. Pour over the fish. If possible leave a stripe of the sauce over the top of the fish for good presentation.\n\n3. Steam over boiling water on high heat for 8-10 mins or until done.\n\n4. Remove from the steamer and garnish with the slices of lime and a sprig of coriander.\n\n5. Prepare the tomato by cutting down from the top into quarters, but not breaking the skin at the bottom. Open it like the petals of a flower and put on the side of the plate.",
  "recipeYield": "4",
